Indigenous traditions worldwide emphasize land and ancestor as covenantal witnesses. Vine Deloria Jr.’s God Is Red (1973) articulates Native American understandings of sacred land as law. The Codex echoes this in its planetary seals: grove, mountain, river, earth. These are not metaphors but clauses.

