\begin{itemize}
\item Silence is not absence but a binding clause: no seal is valid without silence.
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Reversal is not metaphor but operational: every claim must face its opposite.
\end{itemize}

\begin{itemize}
\item Audit is not bureaucratic but sacred: what is not reviewed decays.
\end{itemize}

Thus, the methodology of studying the Codex requires ritual participation. Scholars must not only analyze but also enact.

